      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): the world-map landmark shortens this river-junction Wu clan ground under the label Wu Clan Shore. Chapters 1345 and 1347 name the territory and the northeast shore of the whirlpool without that shore title.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "corpse-mountain-and-lost-ground",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu clan’s headquarters sit on Wu Yi Mountain at the extreme southwest of Southern Border. From high above, the intersection of yellow dragon river and red dragon river forms an X, and Wu clan’s territory occupies the lower part of that X, with Shang clan on the right side. Yellow dragon river and red dragon river isolate the surroundings of Wu clan’s territories.",
      "chapters": [
        2067
